            "id": "m12",
            "title": "Other Indian Uranium Fields: Domiasiat, Rohil, Gogi & Lambapur-Peddagattu",
            "summary": "",
            "theoryHtml": "\n            <h3>India’s Diverse Uranium Portfolio: Domiasiat, Rohil, Gogi & Lambapur</h3>\n            <p>Beyond Jharkhand’s Singhbhum Shear Zone and Andhra Pradesh’s Tummalapalle, the Atomic Minerals Directorate (AMD) has delineated strategic uranium deposits across diverse geological terrains in Meghalaya, Rajasthan, Karnataka, and Telangana.</p>\n\n            <h4>1. Domiasiat / Kylleng-Pyndengsohiong (West Khasi Hills, Meghalaya)</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li><strong>India's Premier Sandstone-Type Deposit:</strong> Located in the Mawthabah area of the West Khasi Hills district of Meghalaya.</li>\n                <li><strong>Exceptional Geological Characteristics:</strong>\n                    <ul>\n                        <li>Hosted within Cretaceous sandstones of the <strong>Lower Mahadek Formation</strong>.</li>\n                        <li>Contains over <strong>10,000 tonnes of uranium resources</strong> with an extraordinarily high average grade (<strong>~0.1% $U_3O_8$</strong>), roughly three times richer than the low-grade ores of Singhbhum and Tummalapalle!</li>\n                        <li>Occurs as a flat-lying, shallow deposit (depth less than 50 meters), amenable to low-cost open-cast mining.</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </li>\n                <li><strong>Socio-Political Stalemate:</strong> Despite its high grade, commercial development remains suspended due to intense local tribal apprehensions regarding radiation safety, environmental protection, and Sixth Schedule land rights.</li>\n            </ul>\n\n            <h4>2. Rohil (Sikar District, Rajasthan)</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li>Located in the North Delhi Fold Belt within an intense sodic metasomatic corridor known as the <strong>'Albitite Zone'</strong>.</li>\n                <li>AMD established over <strong>8,000 tonnes of uranium resources</strong> at Rohil, with additional prospects at Jahaz and Umra (Udaipur). UCIL has initiated groundwork for Rajasthan's first underground uranium mine.</li>\n            </ul>\n\n            <h4>3. Gogi (Yadgir District, Karnataka)</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li>Hosted within phosphatic limestones and fault breccias of the Proterozoic <strong>Bhima Basin</strong>.</li>\n                <li>Although geographically compact, Gogi contains one of the highest-grade uranium ores in India (grading up to <strong>0.15% to 0.2% $U_3O_8$</strong>).</li>\n            </ul>\n\n            <h4>4. Lambapur-Peddagattu & Chitrial (Nalgonda District, Telangana)</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li><strong>Unconformity-Related Uranium:</strong> Located near Nagarjuna Sagar reservoir along the northern boundary of the Cuddapah Basin. Mineralization occurs at the unconformity between the basement granite and the overlying Srisailam Quartzite.</li>\n            </ul>\n        ",
