            "title": "Dr. Homi Bhabha's Three-Stage Nuclear Power Program: The Strategic Thorium Vision",
            "summary": "",
            "theoryHtml": "\n            <h3>Dr. Homi Bhabha's Three-Stage Nuclear Program: The Master Plan for Energy Autonomy</h3>\n            <p>In the 1950s, the visionary architect of India’s atomic energy establishment, <strong>Dr. Homi Jehangir Bhabha</strong>, formulated a brilliant three-stage closed nuclear fuel cycle. Designed specifically to exploit India’s geopolitical reality—<strong>modest domestic uranium reserves but the world’s largest thorium endowment</strong>—the program provides a self-sustaining technological bridge to limitless clean atomic power.</p>\n\n            <h4>1. Stage 1: Pressurized Heavy Water Reactors (PHWRs)</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li><strong>Fuel:</strong> Natural Uranium Dioxide ($UO_2$), containing <strong>0.7% fissile Uranium-235</strong> and <strong>99.3% fertile Uranium-238</strong>.</li>\n                <li><strong>Moderator & Coolant:</strong> Heavy Water (Deuterium Oxide, $D_2O$).</li>\n                <li><strong>Operating Fleet:</strong> Forms the backbone of India's current commercial nuclear power grid, operated by the <em>Nuclear Power Corporation of India Limited (NPCIL)</em> across Rawatbhata (Rajasthan), Tarapur (Maharashtra), Kakrapar (Gujarat), Kaiga (Karnataka), and Narora (UP).</li>\n                <li><strong>The Strategic By-Product:</strong> During operation, fertile $^{238}U$ absorbs neutrons and transmutes into <strong>Plutonium-239 ($^{239}Pu$)</strong>. Spent fuel is chemically reprocessed in specialized DAE plants to extract pure fissile Plutonium-239.</li>\n            </ul>\n\n            <h4>2. Stage 2: Fast Breeder Reactors (FBRs)</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li><strong>Fuel:</strong> Mixed Oxide ($MOX$) consisting of <strong>Plutonium-239 ($^{239}Pu$)</strong> and Uranium-238, surrounded by a blanket of <strong>fertile Thorium-232 ($^{232}Th$)</strong>.</li>\n                <li><strong>Coolant:</strong> Liquid Sodium ($Na$). No moderator is used, allowing fast, unmoderated neutrons to drive fission.</li>\n                <li><strong>The 'Breeder' Magic:</strong> The reactor produces more fissile material than it consumes! Fast neutrons fissioning Plutonium transmute the surrounding Thorium blanket into <strong>fissile Uranium-233 ($^{233}U$)</strong>.</li>\n                <li><strong>Flagship Project:</strong> The <strong>500 MWe Prototype Fast Breeder Reactor (PFBR) at Kalpakkam (Tamil Nadu)</strong>, constructed by <em>BHAVINI (Bharatiya Nabhikiya Vidyut Nigam Limited)</em>. Core loading commenced in March 2024.</li>\n            </ul>\n\n            <h4>3. Stage 3: Advanced Thorium-Based Reactors (AHWR / Thorium-U233 Cycle)</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li><strong>Fuel:</strong> Self-sustaining closed cycle utilizing <strong>Thorium-232 and Uranium-233 ($^{233}U$)</strong>.</li>\n                <li><strong>Advanced Heavy Water Reactor (AHWR):</strong> Conceptualized by BARC; utilizes vertical pressure tubes, natural circulation passive safety systems, and thorium-based fuel.</li>\n                <li><strong>Long-Term Energy Vision:</strong> Unlocks thousands of gigawatt-years of clean, zero-carbon baseload electricity, ensuring India's complete energy sovereignty for over 400 to 500 years!</li>\n            </ul>\n        ",
