            "theoryHtml": "\n            <h3>Diamond Geology in India: The Ancient Golconda Legacy & Panna’s Active Mine</h3>\n            <p><strong>Diamond</strong> is the pure crystalline allotrope of carbon ($C$) formed under extreme mantle temperatures and pressures exceeding 150 kilometers below the Earth’s surface. It defines the absolute benchmark of <strong>Hardness 10 on the Mohs Scale</strong>, possessing the highest thermal conductivity and an extraordinary refractive index (2.42) with high optical dispersion that produces its peerless fire and brilliance.</p>\n\n            <h4>1. India's Incomparable Historic Legacy: The Cradle of World Diamonds</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li>From antiquity until the early 18th century (when Brazilian alluvial diamonds were discovered in 1725), <strong>India was the ONLY known producer of diamonds in the entire world!</strong></li>\n                <li><strong>The Legendary 'Golconda Diamonds':</strong>\n                    <ul>\n                        <li>Panned from the alluvial gravel terraces of the Krishna, Tungabhadra, and Penna river valleys in Andhra Pradesh (Kollur, Paritala, and Vajrakarur).</li>\n                        <li>Sourced the world’s most celebrated historic gemstones: the <strong>Koh-i-Noor</strong> (105.6 carats, British Crown Jewels), the <strong>Hope Diamond</strong> (45.5 carat deep blue diamond), the <strong>Daria-i-Noor</strong> (Iran Crown Jewels), the <strong>Regent Diamond</strong> (Louvre, Paris), and the <strong>Orlov Diamond</strong> (Kremlin, Moscow).</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </li>\n            </ul>\n\n            <h4>2. Majhgawan (Panna, Madhya Pradesh): India’s Sole Active Diamond Mine</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li><strong>The Mine:</strong> Located at Majhgawan in the <strong>Panna district of Madhya Pradesh</strong>, operated by the public sector enterprise <strong>National Mineral Development Corporation (NMDC)</strong>.</li>\n                <li><strong>Unique Distinction:</strong> Majhgawan is the <strong>only mechanized, commercial primary diamond mine operating in the entire continent of Asia!</strong></li>\n                <li><strong>Geological Setting:</strong> Hosted within an ultramafic volcanic pipe (kimberlite/lamproite pipe) that intruded into the Proterozoic Kaimur sandstones of the Vindhyan Supergroup approximately 1.1 billion years ago. Produces around <strong>30,000 carats of gem and industrial diamonds annually</strong>.</li>\n                <li><strong>Alluvial Panna Workings:</strong> Local artisanal miners pan diamonds from shallow conglomerates (Jhiri shales and Itwa sandstones) under licenses granted by the Panna Diamond Mining Office.</li>\n            </ul>\n        ",
